cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "systemgmmkit: Panel-Data Econometrics and Dynamic-Panel GMM Workflows in Python"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software

authors:
  - family-names: Akanbi
    given-names: Oluwajuwon Mayomi

repository-code: "https://github.com/Akanom/systemgmmkit"
url: "https://github.com/Akanom/systemgmmkit"
license: MIT

version: "0.5.13"
date-released: "2026-07-28"

abstract: >
  systemgmmkit is a Python package for applied panel-data econometrics,
  including OLS, pooled OLS, fixed effects, random effects, panel IV / 2SLS,
  Difference GMM, System GMM, dynamic-panel diagnostics, post-estimation,
  visualization, reporting workflows, and ML-style workflow utilities around
  fitted econometric result objects. Version 0.5.13 adds reproducible native-GMM
  and static-estimator performance benchmarks plus opt-in accelerated preparation
  for GMM, fixed effects, and panel IV while preserving the validated mathematics.

keywords:
  - panel data
  - econometrics
  - fixed effects
  - random effects
  - panel IV
  - 2SLS
  - difference GMM
  - system GMM
  - dynamic panel
  - Arellano-Bond
  - Blundell-Bond
  - xtabond2
  - Windmeijer correction
  - post-estimation
  - model comparison
  - forecasting
  - forecast backtesting
  - panel cross-validation
  - machine-learning workflow
  - Python
